# Controlled Remote Administrative Access

Existing SMB sessions were cleared on WIN11-01:

```cmd
net use * /delete /y
```

A controlled connection was then established to the administrative C$ share on WIN11-02:

```cmd
net use \\10.10.10.102\C$ /user:CORP\tadmin *
```

The password was entered interactively rather than placing credentials directly on the command line.

Expected:

```text
The command completed successfully.
```

The administrative share was accessed:

```cmd
dir \\10.10.10.102\C$
```

This generated the controlled activity:

```text
WIN11-01
     |
     | Domain Credentials
     | SMB / TCP 445
     v
WIN11-02
     |
     v
C$ Administrative Share
```

