# Positive Validation

A fresh SMB administrative session was established from WIN11-01 to WIN11-02.

```cmd
net use * /delete /y
```

```cmd
net use \\10.10.10.102\C$ /user:CORP\tadmin *
```

```cmd
dir \\10.10.10.102\C$
```

The resulting network-logon telemetry was ingested into Splunk.

DET-006 was executed against the relevant time window.

Result:

```text
DET-006 TRIGGERED
```

**Positive Validation:** PASS

---

# Negative Validation

The test SMB session was removed:

```cmd
net use \\10.10.10.102\C$ /delete
```

Normal local authentication activity was then generated on WIN11-02 without establishing remote administrative SMB access.

DET-006 was evaluated against the isolated negative-test window.

Result:

```text
DET-006 NOT TRIGGERED
```

**Negative Validation:** PASS

This demonstrated that successful Windows authentication alone did not automatically satisfy the remote administrative logon detection.

